    "result_text": "Done. The full build is green (BUILD SUCCESS, 0 failures/errors).\n\n## Summary\n\nAdded a `checkDigit` field to owner responses, computed as a Luhn check digit over the digits of the `customerCode`.\n\nChanges, each kept to a single responsibility:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `checkDigit` property (integer 0\u20139, `readOnly`) to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field. This matches how every other derived field (`membershipNumber`, `locality`, etc.) is declared.\n\n2. **`model/Luhn.java`** (new) \u2014 a small, pure helper owning only the Luhn algorithm: `checkDigit(String)` over the digits contained in a string, ignoring non-digits. This mirrors the existing domain-helper idiom (`MembershipLevel`, `ContactPreference`, `CityRegion`) and is reusable rather than inlined.\n\n3. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping(target = \"checkDigit\", ...)` and a one-line `checkDigit(Owner)` default method that delegates to `Luhn.checkDigit(owner.getCustomerCode())`, exactly like the other computed-field mappings. No logic was piled into the mapper itself.\n\nThe test recomputes Luhn from the returned `customerCode` and asserts the exact digit \u2014 the implementation uses the same standard algorithm, so they agree.",
